  "id": "COMPOUND:22331 - PROTEIN:2641",
  "verbalization": "Acorone is implicated in the target pathway leading to the EDD domain protein, DegV family through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Acorone acts as a target of multiple compounds, including Pregnenolone, Pubescenone, and 7-Methoxychamanetin, all of which are themselves targets of the EDD domain protein, DegV family. This indicates a potential regulatory or functional relationship where Acorone may influence the activity of the EDD domain protein through these intermediaries. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Acorone modulates the function of the EDD domain protein, possibly through the activation or inhibition of its downstream targets. The recurring involvement of the EDD domain protein, DegV family in the target pathways underscores its role in mediating the effects of these compounds, suggesting a central function in cellular processes that are influenced by Acorone.",
